cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, protocol, or results, please cite it using the
  metadata below. Research prototype — not a medical device.
type: software
title: >-
  BreastUS-CAD: frozen, pre-registered single-shot external validation of a
  breast ultrasound benign/malignant classifier, with deployment-oriented
  follow-up studies and an independent audit trail
version: 1.1-audited
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: Apache-2.0
# concept DOI (resolves to the latest version); version DOIs are listed under identifiers
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22630911
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Thomas
    name-particle: ""
    alias: 王表元
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3066-3298
    email: thomasf45566@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Surgery, National Taiwan University Hospital, Taipei,
      Taiwan
abstract: >-
  Code, protocols, results and audit trail of BreastUS-CAD; frozen model
  weights on Hugging Face. A ViT-B/16 classifier trained on BUS-BRA with
  official patient-level five-fold splits, frozen (tag frozen-v1) and
  validated single-shot on four external cohorts (BrEaST, Curated BUSI,
  GDPH, SYSUCC) under an internally version-controlled pre-registered
  protocol, followed by pre-registered deployment-oriented studies
  (site-specific recalibration, ensemble-disagreement abstention,
  domain-pretrained backbone, leave-one-cohort-out multi-source training),
  an independent adversarial audit (2026-09-06) and two independent
  re-audits (2026-09-11), the item-by-item responses, and post-hoc analyses
  quantifying the disclosed biases. The result tables in RESULTS.md
  recompute from committed CSV/JSON artifacts (wandb-derived and latency
  numbers do not). The internal reference numbers describe one held-out
  checkpoint per image, not the deployed ensemble. Pre-registration was
  internal and not externally time-stamped; see docs/PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - breast ultrasound
  - computer-aided diagnosis
  - external validation
  - pre-registration
  - domain shift
  - calibration
  - vision transformer
  - research prototype
